Subject: Search the full depth of the stack in error recovery

Raise the depth of the stack summary of error recovery.

The copy of the runtime of the tree-sitter-cpp fork has this repair. The fork commit is
27a3142.

The vendored runtime examines 256 stack entries in error recovery, and
the published runtime examines 16. With 16, a file with an error in a
deep construct cannot get back to the translation unit at the end of
the file, and the root node of the tree is ERROR.

On the full corpus, the count of files with an error stays the same.
The files whose error covers 90% of the file or more go from 733 to
430, and the error bytes go from 1.539% to 0.940%. In 124 files the
error shrinks by more than half of the file, and in 2 files it grows.

The patch raises one constant. A better form for upstream puts `#ifndef` around each of the five
limits of parser.c and stack.c, so that a build flag sets them. The five limits are
MAX_VERSION_COUNT, MAX_VERSION_COUNT_OVERFLOW, MAX_SUMMARY_DEPTH, MAX_LINK_COUNT, and
MAX_ITERATOR_COUNT.

Risk for upstream: low. A larger summary costs more time in error recovery only.

The patch applies to the upstream tag v0.27.0, after the patches with a smaller number. The
series compiles with `-Wall -Wextra` and no warning.

The comments hold the marker "(tree-sitter-cpp fork)". Remove the marker before you send the
patch upstream.

diff -ruN a/lib/src/parser.c b/lib/src/parser.c
--- a/lib/src/parser.c	2026-08-30 18:49:12.000000000 +0200
+++ b/lib/src/parser.c	2026-09-15 19:00:45.682701039 +0200
@@ -76,7 +76,10 @@
 
 static const unsigned MAX_VERSION_COUNT = 6;
 static const unsigned MAX_VERSION_COUNT_OVERFLOW = 4;
-static const unsigned MAX_SUMMARY_DEPTH = 16;
+// The depth of the stack that error recovery examines for a state that accepts the lookahead. With
+// 16, a C++ file with an error in a deep construct cannot get back to the translation unit at the end
+// of the file, and its root node is ERROR (tree-sitter-cpp fork).
+static const unsigned MAX_SUMMARY_DEPTH = 256;
 static const unsigned MAX_COST_DIFFERENCE = 18 * ERROR_COST_PER_SKIPPED_TREE;
 static const unsigned OP_COUNT_PER_PARSER_CALLBACK_CHECK = 100;
 
